Track 1: "Who Set the Market Clock Back?"
- Story & Context: The conflict erupted at Bang Phlat Lock when three Port Authority skiffs converged to padlock the floating vegetable stalls twenty minutes before the official dawn horn. Mae Somchit refused to untie her mooring lines, instead driving a ceramic contact mic straight through an overdriven tube preamp and launching a 140 BPM reed barrage that rattled the teeth of every inspector on the jetty. The stench of diesel exhaust and bruised morning coriander hung heavy as the 35Hz drop tore the rusty padlocks clean off the canal chains, swamping the patrol boats in churned silt. Balanced on the prow of her sampan, Somchit gripped her bullhorn and spat the track’s opening salvo into the mist: "You can keep your curfew, we keep the low end."
