Track 2: Mae Pranee's Broken Chronometer
- Story & Context: Mae Pranee recorded this confessional solo track beside Taling Chan Pier after a rusted, waterlogged pocket watch caused her to miss the court hearing regarding the foreclosure of her family’s fruit orchard. She spent three nights tied beneath the corrugated zinc overhang of an abandoned warehouse, freezing as the raw zinc hull chilled her bare knees while she pitch-shifted 1980s real-estate radio jingles into groaning, bottom-heavy dirges. When her market peers gathered their skiffs around her in silent solidarity, Pranee unleashed this weeping, double-reed shriek that sounded like an outboard motor eating its own propeller. Shivering into a grease-spattered condenser microphone, she muttered the hook that became the scene's rallying cry: "My seconds run backward when the reed turns red."
