Track 3: Calendar Pages Choke the Outboard
- Story & Context: By the end of the dry season at Damnoen Saduak, the harbor police completely abandoned their checkpoints after weeks of sleep-deprived standoff against the grandmothers' low-frequency blockade. The final victory rally occurred when dozens of merchant elders drifted past the empty watchtower, gleefully shredding overdue tax notices and municipal summonses into the boat engines' churning propellers. The sound of wood pulp tearing through mechanical impellers was live-sampled and layered beneath a cavernous, sub-bass-heavy bassoon cadence that vibrated the canal bed down to bedrock. As the sunrise burned away the morning smog, the flotilla's unified sound system broadcast the mythic refrain through the reeds: "No bells will strike on our canal."
